{#- Speaker-authored bytes reach this block, so free text is fenced the way the
    baseline accusation_round.j2 / vote_ballot.j2 fence theirs: the whole
    transcript sits inside <transcript> delimiters and each spoken line is
    quoted with its newlines flattened, so no speaker can start a line at
    column 0 and open a section this template's own structure owns (the
    "## Account comparisons" heading below). The structured rows are safe
    without flattening: model_dump_json escapes newlines, and every id in them
    is checked against the roster, room and task ids by
    meetings.public_accounts.validate_public_accounts before the turn records. -#}
## What players said
<transcript>
{% for turn in transcript.turns %}
[{{ turn.turn_id }}] {{ turn.speaker }} said: "{{ turn.free_text | replace('\r', ' ') | replace('\n', ' ') | replace('"', "'") }}"
{% for obs in turn.observations %}
- [turn:{{ turn.turn_id }}:{% if obs.type == "whereabouts" %}whereabouts{% else %}obs{% endif %}:{{ loop.index0 }}] {{ turn.speaker }} stated {{ obs.model_dump_json() }}
{% endfor %}
{% for claim in turn.claims %}
- [turn:{{ turn.turn_id }}:claim:{{ loop.index0 }}] {{ turn.speaker }} stated {{ claim.model_dump_json() }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
</transcript>
## Account comparisons
{% for flag in account_flags %}
- {{ flag.description }}
{% else %}
No account conflict was identified. That does not establish anyone's innocence.
{% endfor %}
